@EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5092

### Get all employees - 200 with a (possibly empty) array
GET {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Accept: application/json

### Get one employee - 200, or 404 if the id does not exist
GET {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1
Accept: application/json

### Create an employee - 201 with a Location header
POST {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@acme-corp.com",
  "departmentId": 7
}

### Create with an unknown department - 400 with ValidationProblemDetails
POST {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@acme-corp.com",
  "departmentId": 999999
}

### Update an employee - 200 with the updated resource, or 404
PUT {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Matthews",
  "email": "john.matthews@acme-corp.com",
  "departmentId": 2
}

### Delete an employee - 204, or 404
DELETE {{EmployeeManager.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees/101

###
### Assignment 02 - the endpoints you must implement.
### Uncomment as you build them. Status is a string, not a number.
